The Secret Life of Pets is a 2016 American animated comedy film directed by
Chris Renaud and written by Brian Lynch, Cinco Paul and Ken Daurio.

11
00:49:47,368 --> 00:49:53,368
Produced by Illumination Entertainment and distributed by Universal Pictures, the film stars the voices of Louis C.K., Eric Stonestreet,
Jenny Slate, Kevin Hart, Ellie Kemper, Lake Bell, Dana Carvey, Hannibal Buress, Bobby Moynihan, Steve Coogan, and Albert Brooks.

12
00:54:18,947 --> 00:54:24,947
Taking place in New York City, the film's plot follows the relationship between
a spoiled terrier named Max and a giant, unruly dog named Duke.

13
00:58:50,526 --> 00:58:56,526
It also follows what other pets do when their owners are gone for the day.

14
01:03:22,105 --> 01:03:28,105
The Secret Life of Pets premiered at the Annecy International Animated Film Festival on
June 16, 2016, and was released in theaters in the United States on July 8.

15
01:07:53,684 --> 01:07:59,684
The film received generally positive reviews and grossed $885.3 million worldwide, making it the
sixth-highest-grossing film of 2016 as well as the year's most profitable release.

16
01:12:25,263 --> 01:12:31,263
A sequel, The Secret Life of Pets 2, was released on June 7, 2019, with
Patton Oswalt taking over the role of Max from Louis C.K.

17
01:16:56,842 --> 01:17:02,842
The film explores themes of bunny, pet, anthropomorphism, dog, animals.

18
01:21:28,421 --> 01:21:34,421
The tone is lighthearted.
